1
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:04,550
You're the only one here so far, Yagami?

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,830
Hey, Utomiya-kun.

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:10,990
I had a feeling you'd be
the Class C representative.

4
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:13,110
Though I'm not convinced
I'm cut out for leadership.

5
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:17,660
I'm sure the others realized
how responsible you were.

6
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,940
We've lost one of our own.

7
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:22,980
I take that loss extremely seriously.

8
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:26,420
I didn't expect Hatano-kun
to get expelled, either.

9
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:28,500
It's a terrible shame.

10
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,540
Yes.

11
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,600
Do you think Hosen will come?

12
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,090
I'd give it 50-50 odds.

13
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:37,250
I'd bet on no.

14
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:41,150
Class D won't work with anyone
unless they get points out of it.

15
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:42,690
I think that's why he might come.

16
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:47,730
If he doesn't, we'll form our own
group without Class D for sure.

17
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:52,920
Far from being in demand then,
they'll be left out in the cold.

18
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:55,170
Hey, Riku, Takuya!

19
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:56,730
I knew it'd be you two.

20
00:00:56,730 --> 00:01:00,740
They're still making you do
all the dirty work, Osamu-kun?

21
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:04,230
Our leader hates the dirty work.

22
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:06,000
That makes me the fall guy.

23
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:08,490
We just waiting on Kazuomi?

24
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:11,700
Wouldn't it be better for
us to work without him?

25
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,880
The deserted island test will require
skills other than pure academics.

26
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:18,060
Class D may be the
lowest-ranked class overall,

27
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:20,140
but they're first in Physical
Ability by a narrow margin.

28
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:24,630
I think they could play a crucial
role in group formation.

29
00:01:24,630 --> 00:01:26,760
I get what you're saying, Riku.

30
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,650
Our Class A is annoyed about Kazuomi's
attitude of demanding points

31
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:32,790
in exchange for cooperation, too.

32
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:35,980
But I don't think we should
count them out just yet.

33
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,290
I acknowledge that Class D
has a great deal to offer,

34
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:42,840
but I don't think it's worth
trying to curry favor with Hosen.

35
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:47,020
Looks like you won't get your wish, Riku.

36
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:05,360
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

37
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:15,970
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

38
00:03:21,010 --> 00:03:23,220
So you're ready to pay up, are you?

39
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:25,100
Is that supposed to be funny?

40
00:03:25,390 --> 00:03:28,220
We're not paying you a single point.

41
00:03:26,730 --> 00:03:29,150
#7 Plotting

42
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,100
Let's all settle down, now.

43
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:33,890
We can't negotiate if we start
out at each other's throats.

44
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:37,230
Now that we're all here,
let's get started, then.

45
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:40,240
I didn't say I was ready to start!

46
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:45,120
Hosen, I'm going to ask you
to refrain from violence here.

47
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:48,120
Oh? You gonna stop me, then?

48
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:50,230
I will if I have to.

49
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:51,870
Sounds fun.

50
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:54,630
Show me what you can do, then!

51
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:57,590
This is ridiculous.

52
00:03:57,590 --> 00:04:01,080
But if that's what you want,
I'll respond in kind...

53
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:07,440
on the condition that you leave
my classmates alone forever.

54
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,220
Hey, now, what's that supposed to mean?

55
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:14,120
I know who got Hatano expelled.

56
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,560
And you think it was me?

57
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,400
Who else could it be?

58
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,530
Calm down, you two!

59
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:23,450
Right now, we need to focus on the
deserted island survival game.

60
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:26,490
Did I say I was here to talk about that?

61
00:04:26,490 --> 00:04:30,370
Then did you just come here to kill time?

62
00:04:30,370 --> 00:04:31,950
What if I did?

63
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:36,460
I refuse to believe you're that stupid.

64
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:41,350
Both the second- and third-years
have been through this test before.

65
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:45,060
We need to recognize that we're
at a severe disadvantage.

66
00:04:45,470 --> 00:04:49,620
If we can't work together,
they'll eat us all alive.

67
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:52,350
That's coward talk, Yagami.

68
00:04:52,690 --> 00:04:56,460
I'm not afraid of the upperclassmen.
I can crush 'em all.

69
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:00,320
Not everyone is as blessed as you are.

70
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,780
The fact of the matter
is that first-years,

71
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:04,570
as a whole, are at a disadvantage.

72
00:05:04,810 --> 00:05:07,740
I think it's necessary for
first-years to work together

73
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:12,450
and make at least one
powerful group of four.

74
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:14,900
A group of students who

75
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:19,730
can easily compete with the
upperclassmen, like you said.

76
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:24,210
You're proposing that we don't
compete with each other for class points

77
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:25,130
this time?

78
00:05:25,410 --> 00:05:29,900
Yes. Unlike the upperclassman, who don't
have much time before graduation,

79
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:32,580
we'll have more than enough
time for that moving forward.

80
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:36,390
So we should abandon this
as a race for class points.

81
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:39,900
I'm not sure that's sufficient reason
for us to team up with each other.

82
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:43,750
We'll have far more to lose if
the upperclassmen trample us.

83
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:46,070
Wait a minute, Takuya.

84
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,020
Why just one group?

85
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:51,080
If the idea is to have groups
meet up for the main event,

86
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:54,610
wouldn't it be better to
have multiple strong groups?

87
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:56,910
You're right, of course.

88
00:05:56,910 --> 00:06:01,360
But if we do that from the start,
we risk dividing our power.

89
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,620
It's important to make the
strongest possible group of four

90
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:06,460
that can definitely take first place.

91
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,690
Since the upperclassmen

92
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:10,930
can only have a maximum of three people
from three classes working together.

93
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:15,860
And if we can take first place, we don't
have to worry about the rest at all?

94
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:19,060
Even if Hosen-kun refuses and
it's just our three classes,

95
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:21,490
we'll just use the same strategy
as the other grade years.

96
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:24,220
We first-years are given the privilege

97
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,060
of forming small groups
of up to four people.

98
00:06:27,410 --> 00:06:30,450
It would be a waste to
just throw that away.

99
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,950
So I want you to help me.

100
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,450
Sure, I'm willing to help out.

101
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:39,580
What are you up to, Hosen?

102
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:41,580
Why should I be up to something?

103
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:46,470
You made your cute little request for my
help, and I'm willing to entertain it.

104
00:06:46,470 --> 00:06:48,310
What are your conditions?

105
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:50,520
For the large group when we get there,

106
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:54,320
I want the two empty slots
to be Class D students.

107
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,350
That's my must-have.

108
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,550
What?

109
00:06:57,550 --> 00:07:01,730
But we still don't know if we'll get
to choose our large groups or not.

110
00:07:01,970 --> 00:07:05,730
I told you, that's my must-have.

111
00:07:05,730 --> 00:07:09,550
I see. So if we can't let
in two Class D students,

112
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:11,990
we'll have to complete the
test with just the four.

113
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:14,110
Don't mess around, Hosen.

114
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:15,400
I'm not messing around.

115
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,740
If you don't like it, you can drop out.

116
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,290
You son of a...

117
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:21,450
Calm down, Utomiya-kun.

118
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:24,290
I think his conditions are acceptable.

119
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:28,440
Our priority should be unity
between the four of us.

120
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,680
If we give him an inch now,
he'll take a mile later.

121
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:36,310
And if we let Class D go now,
you think that will change his attitude?

122
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:37,670
Well...

123
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:42,280
The most important thing now is
that the first-years win this test.

124
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,510
We should set aside everything else.

125
00:07:44,510 --> 00:07:46,630
I agree with him, Riku.

126
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:50,190
I understand how you feel,
but first-year unity has to come first.

127
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:54,820
So as long as you get that,
you're fine with anything else, Hosen?

128
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:57,730
Do what you want.

129
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:09,960
So, are we heading to Yukimoo's room?

130
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:13,570
I'm fine with it, but we're
going to study, not hang out.

131
00:08:13,570 --> 00:08:15,240
Yeah, I know.

132
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,700
Ayanokoji-kun!

133
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,600
Are you free for a minute?

134
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:19,680
What is it?

135
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:24,290
There's a first-year who
wants to speak to you.

136
00:08:24,290 --> 00:08:26,560
Do you think you'd be able to see them?

137
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,500
What's this, Kiyo-pon?

138
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:31,440
Think some little kohai
has a crush on you?

139
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:34,570
I-Is that what it is?!

140
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:39,030
If it is, I'm afraid
I can't give my blessing.

141
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:40,290
Is that what it is?

142
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:46,300
Well, it's actually a boy
who wants to talk to you...

143
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:47,920
Sorry.

144
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,420
Seems fine to me.

145
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:52,920
It's good to make more inroads
with the first-years.

146
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:58,550
Yeah. Since our group isn't
exactly outgoing, either.

147
00:08:58,550 --> 00:09:03,250
Y-Yes. It's fine with me if you go, then.

148
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:05,320
All right.

149
00:09:07,770 --> 00:09:10,300
Looks like he's coming.

150
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,930
Let's wait here.

151
00:09:11,930 --> 00:09:16,700
It seems like you've gotten close
with the first-years already.

152
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,450
Huh? Well, it's already July.

153
00:09:19,450 --> 00:09:22,080
We've had plenty of time.

154
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:26,770
I'm sure you've made a few friends
among the first-years yourself!

155
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:29,840
I wouldn't go that far just yet.

156
00:09:30,090 --> 00:09:31,960
R-Really?

157
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:35,220
Well, no need to rush, I suppose.

158
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,750
There's lots of time left!

159
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,680
Kushida-senpai!

160
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:42,540
This is the one who wanted to
meet you. His name is Yagami-kun.

161
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,430
It's a pleasure to meet
you, Ayanokoji-senpai.

162
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:49,090
Thank you for making
time to speak with me.

163
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:52,240
You're in Class 1-B, right?

164
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,320
Yes!

165
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,060
I'm Yagami Takuya!

166
00:09:57,110 --> 00:10:01,830
I actually have to tell you something.

167
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:07,840
Are you aware of the extremely limited
special test that's been offered

168
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,750
to the first-years?

169
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:15,160
Um, I'm afraid I haven't
heard anything about this...

170
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:17,340
Do you mind if I talk in front of her?

171
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:19,710
I have no right to stop you.

172
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:25,720
Soon after we came to the school,
we got a communique from President Nagumo.

173
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,930
Whoever gets you expelled before

174
00:10:28,930 --> 00:10:33,980
the second term begins will
be paid 20 million points.

175
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:36,910
What? You have to expel Ayanokoji-kun?

176
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:40,010
And 20 million... That's so much!

177
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:42,020
Is that really allowed?

178
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:46,980
I understand now that this was an
extremely unusual special test.

179
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:53,240
I also have no interest in getting
rewarded for sabotaging someone else,

180
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:55,670
so I have no intention of participating.

181
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:59,350
But why Ayanokoji-kun?

182
00:10:59,350 --> 00:11:03,120
The president said he was chosen
at random from the second-years.

183
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,390
But didn't it seem strange
to have a special test that

184
00:11:06,390 --> 00:11:08,200
wasn't officially issued by the school?

185
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:15,590
Acting Chairman Tsukishiro was present
when the president told us about it.

186
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:20,180
It seemed like a legitimate setting
in which to be issued a special test.

187
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,410
The acting chairman was there?

188
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:25,580
Yeah, I guess that does seem legitimate...

189
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:31,030
In attendance from Class 1-A were
Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyo-kun.

190
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:33,070
From Class B, it was me.

191
00:11:33,070 --> 00:11:35,230
From Class C, it was Utomiya Riku-kun.

192
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:41,220
And from Class D, it was Hosen
Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san.

193
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:44,190
What made you decide to tell me about it?

194
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:48,600
I heard that Hosen-kun took
his chance at it, but failed.

195
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:52,310
And he did it in the most
barbaric way possible.

196
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,430
I won't deny that.

197
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,620
One other thing.

198
00:11:57,190 --> 00:12:01,100
I determined that if I don't act,
it's possible that your classmate,

199
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:05,940
Kushida-senpai, could
end up harmed, as well.

200
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:11,640
I appreciate the concern, but it could
be dangerous for you to tell me this.

201
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:13,780
Will you be all right, Yagami-kun?

202
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:15,380
If this gets out...

203
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:17,690
It's okay, Kushida-senpai.

204
00:12:17,690 --> 00:12:20,510
He didn't mention anything
about penalties.

205
00:12:20,510 --> 00:12:24,510
And I'm prepared to be hated by a
certain segment of the first-years.

206
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:27,890
We'll have to fight the other
classes sooner or later anyway.

207
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:31,680
Please be careful, Ayanokoji-senpai.

208
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:32,670
All right.

209
00:12:32,670 --> 00:12:36,980
So, is there anyone you're
particularly worried about?

210
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:38,940
Let me see.

211
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,530
Hosen-kun seems like the
most likely subject,

212
00:12:41,530 --> 00:12:44,250
but if I had to name one in particular...

213
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,360
No, I won't say it.

214
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:50,370
Why not? Now I'm curious!

215
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:55,380
If I give their name now,
you'll put a target on their back.

216
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:58,630
As a fellow first-year,
I don't think that would be fair.

217
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:01,380
And I'm not completely certain
of their character yet.

218
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:05,300
During the upcoming special
test, I want to see for myself

219
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,760
if they're dangerous or not.

220
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:10,510
You be careful now, Yagami-kun.

221
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:11,610
I will.

222
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:19,020
And... I'm okay to wait until
after the test is over,

223
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,780
but I want to talk to you, Kushida-senpai.

224
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:24,260
Oh, okay.

225
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,070
I wonder what it could be about!

226
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:29,380
That's a fine kohai you've got.

227
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:32,790
Yeah. I'm really not worthy of him...

228
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:36,790
Not that I'm happy about it.

229
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:40,840
Yagami-kun knows about my past.

230
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:42,920
And?

231
00:13:43,230 --> 00:13:46,680
I'll need to get rid of him soon.

232
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,600
Getting rid of a lowerclassman

233
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,300
will be harder than getting
rid of me or Horikita.

234
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:54,440
That depends on how I go about it.

235
00:13:54,440 --> 00:14:00,060
The smarter someone thinks they are,
the more easily they're disposed of.

236
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:03,900
You and Horikita-san aren't exceptions.

237
00:14:04,330 --> 00:14:07,820
I thought we had a truce.

238
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:10,320
Sure, I'll be a good girl for now!

239
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:13,590
See you later, Ayanokoji-kun!

240
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:26,090
Hey. Can we talk?

241
00:14:26,810 --> 00:14:29,970
I'm sorry to approach you
under these conditions.

242
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:32,350
What do you want to talk about?

243
00:14:32,350 --> 00:14:34,420
It's about Hosen Kazuomi.

244
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:38,100
You've experienced his uncooperative
attitude by now, I'm sure.

245
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:42,480
We want to deal him a blow
during the survival game.

246
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:46,400
He doesn't have a lot of
private points at the moment.

247
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:51,100
If we force him to drop out early,
he won't be able to pay the penalty.

248
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:54,240
So you want to get Hosen expelled?

249
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,400
Hell yes!

250
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,310
I mean, yes, that's correct.

251
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:00,500
Mind if I ask why?

252
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:05,060
Another member of Class 1-C,
Hatano, was expelled.

253
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:08,380
I'm positive that Hosen was involved.

254
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,630
And you want revenge?

255
00:15:10,630 --> 00:15:14,010
I would be lying if I said
I didn't hold a grudge.

256
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:18,020
But the most important thing is
to prevent any future expulsions.

257
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:22,270
Yeah. We lost a hundred
class points from that.

258
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:26,070
So, what does that have to do with me?

259
00:15:26,070 --> 00:15:29,250
Hosen has refused to work with
anyone outside his class.

260
00:15:29,250 --> 00:15:32,950
But you partnered with him
during the April test.

261
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:37,320
So you think I have special access to him?

262
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,730
Please help me.

263
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:44,130
It's hard to agree when we don't
yet know what the test entails.

264
00:15:44,130 --> 00:15:47,580
Then will you agree to consider the offer?

265
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:51,300
If we can eliminate Hosen
early and get him expelled,

266
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,480
I'll pay you a considerable reward.

267
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:57,350
You haven't considered that
I might be Hosen's ally?

268
00:15:57,350 --> 00:15:58,570
Well...

269
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,100
That wound on your hand.

270
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:07,500
You got it in a fight with
Hosen-kun, didn't you?

271
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,610
What makes you think that?

272
00:16:09,610 --> 00:16:14,070
Because we were after the
20-million-point bounty, too.

273
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:15,320
I see.

274
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,760
Is that why you approached
me that evening,

275
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,430
pretending to search for a partner?

276
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:21,000
That's right.

277
00:16:21,310 --> 00:16:23,030
But I doubt you had a way

278
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:25,910
of getting just me expelled if
I had agreed to work with you.

279
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:28,450
Don't know what to tell you there.

280
00:16:28,450 --> 00:16:30,430
I apologize about that.

281
00:16:30,430 --> 00:16:32,960
But we've withdrawn from that test.

282
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,010
Why?

283
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:37,540
Even if we did succeed
at having you expelled,

284
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:40,450
that would quickly become
known throughout the school.

285
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:44,140
We'd make an enemy of
the entire Class 2-D.

286
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:48,400
Wouldn't getting Hosen expelled
result in the same?

287
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,410
That seems doubtful.

288
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:55,060
I suspect more of his classmates
will be glad to be rid of him.

289
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,780
Just keep it in mind, would you?

290
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,540
All we want is to see Hosen expelled.

291
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:03,490
Tick tock.

292
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:07,540
I really hate that noisy watch of yours.

293
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,530
Oh, shut up.

294
00:17:09,530 --> 00:17:12,660
You don't know how much this
watch is worth, do you?

295
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:15,930
I don't waste my time researching
the prices of things I hate.

296
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,260
So, what did you want?

297
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:20,580
It's about the deserted island test.

298
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,490
Partner up with me, Amasawa.

299
00:17:22,490 --> 00:17:25,000
You want my help, huh?

300
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,350
And on a deserted island...

301
00:17:27,350 --> 00:17:29,310
You got sexy things in mind?

302
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:32,590
Wanna see my panties?

303
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:34,360
I'll give you a glimpse if you'd like.

304
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:38,340
You think I won't hit a woman?

305
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:41,870
Relax. I'm sure you'd
hit absolutely anyone.

306
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:45,000
Then you better cut
the bullshit real fast.

307
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,430
Let me ask you this, then.

308
00:17:48,430 --> 00:17:52,130
Why include me in your plan?

309
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:57,930
You've got the guts to dive headfirst
into getting Ayanokoji expelled.

310
00:17:57,930 --> 00:18:02,890
For a 20-million-point jackpot?
Who wouldn't?

311
00:18:03,150 --> 00:18:04,890
So, what are you offering?

312
00:18:05,430 --> 00:18:07,890
We're supposed to be equals here.

313
00:18:08,110 --> 00:18:10,650
We discussed that earlier, didn't we?

314
00:18:10,650 --> 00:18:16,650
I see. A group thought up by
Hosen-kun, including Nanase-chan...

315
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,530
But who's our fourth?

316
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,300
Don't need one.

317
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:24,160
The winner of the deserted island
test will be the three of us.

318
00:18:24,410 --> 00:18:26,420
You seem very confident about that.

319
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:29,790
But what about the plan to have
the four classes work together

320
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:33,420
to make the strongest possible group?

321
00:18:33,730 --> 00:18:38,940
I figured one of you two would
be the Class D representative.

322
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:42,930
That's up to me, the leader
of Class D, to decide.

323
00:18:42,930 --> 00:18:44,970
You see what I'm getting at?

324
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:48,790
You're going to send in a lesser
being as your representative?

325
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:51,770
You're picking a fight from all sides.

326
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,350
As long as we send in someone
sufficiently smart or strong,

327
00:18:55,350 --> 00:18:57,060
it won't seem suspicious.

328
00:18:57,590 --> 00:19:02,940
And Hosen-kun joining the four-class
group would cause problems of its own.

329
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:07,000
Yeah, he doesn't seem
like the teamwork type.

330
00:19:07,410 --> 00:19:10,930
So, let's get down to brass tacks.
How much will you pay me?

331
00:19:10,930 --> 00:19:12,790
We won't be paying you.

332
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,630
I will stress again that we are equals.

333
00:19:16,630 --> 00:19:22,030
But our contributions won't
be equal, now, will they?

334
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:26,640
I'm positive I can contribute in any
setting, deserted island included.

335
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,830
It'll likely require stamina.

336
00:19:28,830 --> 00:19:32,920
Can our sweet little doll
Nanase-chan hope to keep up?

337
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,400
Would you like to try me?

338
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:37,570
Well, you're quite bold.

339
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:42,160
Hey, maybe you've got
what it takes after all.

340
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:45,160
I just love strong women.

341
00:19:45,450 --> 00:19:49,490
You seem rather exceptional yourself.

342
00:19:49,490 --> 00:19:51,290
Oh, do I?

343
00:19:54,010 --> 00:19:59,060
Me, Nanase, and you will
form a three-person group.

344
00:19:59,060 --> 00:19:59,800
Got that?

345
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:03,910
I'll admit that Nanase-chan
has the physicality.

346
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:07,930
But I'd still like a bonus
for helping you out.

347
00:20:07,930 --> 00:20:10,560
You think pretty highly of yourself, huh?

348
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:15,440
Tell me, then. What do you
want besides the group reward?

349
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:21,720
I want all the points for
expelling Ayanokoji-senpai.

350
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:23,590
That's my condition.

351
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:27,140
Man, you're pretty damn full of yourself.

352
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,540
Can't agree to that.

353
00:20:29,850 --> 00:20:32,330
I guess it'll be a no from me, then.

354
00:20:32,330 --> 00:20:35,170
But are you sure you can
afford to lose my interest?

355
00:20:35,170 --> 00:20:37,340
You're picking fights on all sides.

356
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:41,830
Might be hard with no one you
can trust besides Nanase-chan.

357
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:47,250
Of course, if we expel Ayanokoji-senpai,
all the glory will go to you.

358
00:20:47,590 --> 00:20:49,100
That's enough, isn't it?

359
00:20:49,490 --> 00:20:51,310
You don't need to accept her terms.

360
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:55,110
If we give the whole 20 million
to Class A, moving forward—

361
00:20:55,110 --> 00:20:56,480
Oh, shut up.

362
00:20:56,990 --> 00:21:00,230
Amasawa, you can have the reward.

363
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:02,260
Aw, thanks!

364
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:06,240
I've always thought a man's most
appealing trait is his generosity.

365
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:09,490
Well, see you at the test.

366
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:12,960
Are you sure about this?

367
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:16,070
She seems like a backstabber to me.

368
00:21:16,070 --> 00:21:20,000
I haven't trusted you
or her from the start.

369
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:22,660
Why work with her, then?

370
00:21:23,270 --> 00:21:25,790
She's not like the other
trash around here.

371
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:29,650
Like you, she's got hidden depths.

372
00:21:29,650 --> 00:21:31,510
That may be true.

373
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:35,030
But 20 million feels like
a steep price to pay.

374
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:39,740
Who gives a damn about
some verbal agreement?

375
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:44,630
If I get that guy expelled,
the reward gets paid out to me.

376
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:48,280
She can cry all she wants
about it. I won't give a damn.

377
00:21:48,510 --> 00:21:50,160
You're truly cruel.

378
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:54,490
Ayanokoji, Ryuen, all the
unwashed masses out there...

379
00:21:54,490 --> 00:21:58,040
I'll crush anyone who comes after me.

380
00:21:58,350 --> 00:22:02,800
This school's got such crazy rules...

381
00:22:03,110 --> 00:22:05,050
and I'm loving it!
